1
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:24,003 --> 00:00:25,255
Your treatment…

3
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:27,841
Next time.

4
00:00:30,552 --> 00:00:33,304
You should have gotten it.
You went through all that trouble.

5
00:00:34,472 --> 00:00:35,598
It wasn't any trouble.

6
00:00:37,225 --> 00:00:40,103
You gave me socks
so my feet wouldn't get cold

7
00:00:40,186 --> 00:00:43,273
and loaded up the MP3 player with music
so I wouldn't get carsick.

8
00:00:44,357 --> 00:00:45,400
You did all that.

9
00:00:58,163 --> 00:01:00,707
You and your grandma…

10
00:01:00,790 --> 00:01:03,668
I know how special a bond you share.

11
00:01:05,128 --> 00:01:07,380
So I know how you must feel right now.

12
00:01:09,174 --> 00:01:12,510
Nothing is more painful
than seeing a loved one in pain.

13
00:01:16,681 --> 00:01:20,351
No matter what the results are,
there'll be a way.

14
00:01:22,103 --> 00:01:24,022
Whatever it is, I'll be here with you.

15
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:28,276
So don't worry too much.

16
00:01:31,571 --> 00:01:32,405
Okay?

17
00:01:46,252 --> 00:01:48,546
I'm really sorry, sir.

18
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:52,425
I didn't think
Prosecutor Go would just not show up…

19
00:01:52,508 --> 00:01:55,094
I'll do whatever it takes
to set up another meeting.

20
00:02:02,602 --> 00:02:03,937
Sir.

21
00:02:14,614 --> 00:02:15,573
Yes, that's her.

22
00:02:15,657 --> 00:02:17,242
That's Prosecutor Go.

23
00:02:17,325 --> 00:02:18,159
Yes.

24
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:33,258
She was alive.

25
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:35,885
This bitch was alive.

26
00:02:37,053 --> 00:02:38,680
But why has she been so quiet?

27
00:02:41,849 --> 00:02:43,643
Didn't you say it wasn't just the watch

28
00:02:44,227 --> 00:02:46,229
that could put
Mayor Ju and me behind bars?

29
00:02:46,312 --> 00:02:49,065
Yes, she definitely said that,

30
00:02:49,983 --> 00:02:52,777
but I'm not really sure
why she hasn't shown up yet.

31
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:54,696
One thing did seem strange.

32
00:02:54,779 --> 00:02:58,032
When I was on the phone with her,
she called me Mr. Gwak Chi-hyeon.

33
00:02:58,116 --> 00:02:59,951
She's never once called me that--

34
00:03:11,838 --> 00:03:13,381
If you want to keep breathing,

35
00:03:14,674 --> 00:03:16,384
find Go Ji-won as soon as possible.

36
00:03:17,385 --> 00:03:18,219
Yes.

37
00:03:20,555 --> 00:03:22,432
I understand, sir.

38
00:03:39,699 --> 00:03:42,160
GO JI-WON 2

39
00:03:45,705 --> 00:03:47,874
This is driving me nuts.

40
00:03:52,086 --> 00:03:53,004
An ex-boyfriend?

41
00:03:53,671 --> 00:03:56,591
Okay, so in a nutshell,

42
00:03:56,674 --> 00:03:59,469
you remembered a guy
who could either be your ex

43
00:03:59,552 --> 00:04:01,596
or the guy you cheated on Tae-ha with.

44
00:04:01,679 --> 00:04:04,974
So, whether or not to tell Tae-ha

45
00:04:05,058 --> 00:04:08,853
is the critical question at hand. Correct?

46
00:04:08,936 --> 00:04:09,812
Yes.

47
00:04:09,896 --> 00:04:12,690
I don't want to keep secrets from Tae-ha,

48
00:04:12,774 --> 00:04:15,610
and it's a good thing
that I remembered something,

49
00:04:15,693 --> 00:04:17,153
so I do want to tell him.

50
00:04:18,446 --> 00:04:21,240
But it just had to be a memory of a guy.

51
00:04:21,324 --> 00:04:23,618
Goodness, I see what you're saying.

52
00:04:23,701 --> 00:04:26,662
If you ask me,
I don't think you should ever tell him.

53
00:04:26,746 --> 00:04:29,207
As a rule of thumb,
both corpses and talk of exes

54
00:04:29,290 --> 00:04:31,501
are best kept buried deep.

55
00:04:31,584 --> 00:04:33,127
-That's exactly right.
-Right.

56
00:04:33,211 --> 00:04:36,297
Surely, Tae-ha won't think
that he's your first boyfriend,

57
00:04:36,381 --> 00:04:40,551
but even if he doesn't,
actually hearing about a past guy…

58
00:04:41,135 --> 00:04:46,015
It'll start to eat away at him
like stock that's plummeted, you know?

59
00:04:46,099 --> 00:04:49,227
Just when he's about to forget,
it'll pop right into his mind.

60
00:04:49,310 --> 00:04:51,604
Or he'll get all worked up
in the dead of night.

61
00:04:51,687 --> 00:04:56,109
Or in the middle of a meal,
he'll suddenly start burning up inside!

62
00:04:56,192 --> 00:04:58,361
Did your husband dabble in stocks again?

63
00:04:58,444 --> 00:05:02,323
I'm going to stomp on that damn ape!

64
00:05:02,407 --> 00:05:04,784
Then I guess I shouldn't tell him.

65
00:05:04,867 --> 00:05:06,536
-Yeah.
-That's smart of you.

66
00:05:06,619 --> 00:05:10,998
Then let's all agree to lock this up
and throw away the key.

67
00:05:11,624 --> 00:05:12,625
Okay.

68
00:05:13,501 --> 00:05:14,460
-Please eat.
-Okay.

69
00:05:25,096 --> 00:05:26,973
I assume you didn't leave any crumbs.

70
00:05:27,849 --> 00:05:28,975
Yes, sir.

71
00:05:32,061 --> 00:05:34,105
Jang Tae-ha deceived me.

72
00:05:35,189 --> 00:05:37,358
He sure learned that from Hong Do-yeop.

73
00:05:37,942 --> 00:05:41,070
I think I performed well
thanks to everything Coach Hong taught me.

74
00:05:41,821 --> 00:05:46,367
I'll now do my best at the Olympics
with the Taegeuk emblem on my chest.

75
00:05:46,451 --> 00:05:51,581
I cherish Jang Tae-ha
as if he were made from my own rib.

76
00:05:52,331 --> 00:05:54,750
And soon, not only me

77
00:05:54,834 --> 00:06:00,006
but all of Korea will come to cherish him
as a great athlete.

78
00:06:08,931 --> 00:06:11,767
AN MENTAL HEALTH CLINIC

79
00:06:22,361 --> 00:06:24,447
-You're here.
-You told me to come.

80
00:06:25,281 --> 00:06:27,033
Right, I did.

81
00:06:27,116 --> 00:06:28,075
Have a seat.

82
00:06:29,285 --> 00:06:31,954
Sit down for a bit. I won't keep you long.

83
00:06:45,968 --> 00:06:46,802
What's this?

84
00:06:46,886 --> 00:06:48,054
Take a look.

85
00:06:55,061 --> 00:06:57,146
You like G-Dragon's music.

86
00:06:57,230 --> 00:06:59,232
His songs are in there.

87
00:07:00,191 --> 00:07:04,820
And it's not great
to have cold feet, so I…

88
00:07:04,904 --> 00:07:06,364
You called me to give me this?

89
00:07:07,323 --> 00:07:09,325
-What?
-Who uses MP3 players these days?

90
00:07:09,408 --> 00:07:11,202
I can afford a music subscription.

91
00:07:11,786 --> 00:07:14,539
And what's with these?
I already run hot as it is.

92
00:07:16,165 --> 00:07:18,668
Don't call me over
for stupid things like this.

93
00:07:18,751 --> 00:07:20,628
Just approve my resignation already.

94
00:07:26,384 --> 00:07:27,343
What the heck?

95
00:07:27,843 --> 00:07:32,473
Jang Tae-ha got us to turn the car around
with this. Why didn't it work for me?

96
00:07:40,356 --> 00:07:41,774
This looks delicious.

97
00:07:42,525 --> 00:07:43,568
It looks good.

98
00:07:45,736 --> 00:07:49,907
The air is so fresh. It's lovely here.

99
00:07:49,991 --> 00:07:52,827
How are you feeling, ma'am?
Are you feeling better?

100
00:07:52,910 --> 00:07:55,997
Well, it reminds me of the war. It's nice.

101
00:07:58,541 --> 00:07:59,709
Should we go elsewhere?

102
00:07:59,792 --> 00:08:03,671
It took you over an hour
to set up that tent.

103
00:08:03,754 --> 00:08:05,506
It'd be a waste. Let's just stay.

104
00:08:06,173 --> 00:08:07,008
Sure.

105
00:08:08,968 --> 00:08:11,554
-I'll go buy a new one. Is it out of gas?
-No, I'll go.

106
00:08:12,471 --> 00:08:15,016
Hurry up and get things ready.
She's hungry.

107
00:08:25,985 --> 00:08:27,236
Goodness.

108
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:30,865
We should be grilling meat
at a place like this.

109
00:08:31,365 --> 00:08:34,577
You can't have grilled meat.
Don't you know what condition you're in?

110
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:37,455
How much longer
do you think I have to live?

111
00:08:37,538 --> 00:08:38,372
Grandma.

112
00:08:38,456 --> 00:08:42,209
Why would you even
say something like that?

113
00:08:44,045 --> 00:08:47,548
So don't spend money on my treatment.

114
00:08:48,549 --> 00:08:49,842
-Okay?
-No.

115
00:08:51,052 --> 00:08:54,263
I'll save you no matter what.

116
00:08:54,764 --> 00:08:58,976
You've been saving me my whole life.
What more is there to save?

117
00:09:00,603 --> 00:09:04,649
I lost your mom to an illness
just when I was getting attached.

118
00:09:04,732 --> 00:09:06,108
Just my luck.

119
00:09:07,151 --> 00:09:09,570
I wouldn't have missed a thing
even if I died back then.

120
00:09:09,654 --> 00:09:12,490
A truly miserable life.

121
00:09:13,407 --> 00:09:16,202
But you breathed life into me.

122
00:09:17,286 --> 00:09:23,459
Even when life threw me
mountains upon mountains of sorrow,

123
00:09:24,627 --> 00:09:27,672
I gritted my teeth and lived on
because of you.

124
00:09:28,381 --> 00:09:31,300
So it's enough now.

125
00:09:31,384 --> 00:09:34,345
It's time you stopped saving me.

126
00:09:36,555 --> 00:09:38,933
For the rest of my days,

127
00:09:39,016 --> 00:09:42,895
instead of reeling in pain
from that excruciating treatment,

128
00:09:43,771 --> 00:09:47,566
and instead of staring at the faces
of doctors I don't even know,

129
00:09:48,359 --> 00:09:53,739
I want to go back to making taffy,
the thing that kept food on the table.

130
00:09:55,491 --> 00:09:56,826
You, my precious baby.

131
00:09:57,827 --> 00:09:59,912
My pitiful Song-wol.

132
00:10:00,413 --> 00:10:04,417
And the villagers who are kind-hearted
once you get to know them.

133
00:10:05,209 --> 00:10:06,252
All of you.

134
00:10:07,336 --> 00:10:11,340
I want to spend my last days
taking you all in.

135
00:10:13,759 --> 00:10:15,010
Tae-ha.

136
00:10:16,011 --> 00:10:20,141
Please let me do that, okay?

137
00:10:22,435 --> 00:10:23,936
Don't cry.

138
00:10:24,437 --> 00:10:29,066
It breaks my heart to see
that handsome face of yours downcast.

139
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:35,990
By the way,

140
00:10:36,866 --> 00:10:41,412
are you thinking of marrying that girl?

141
00:10:44,707 --> 00:10:48,210
My whole body aches
from walking around all day.

142
00:10:48,294 --> 00:10:49,336
Goodness.

143
00:10:52,214 --> 00:10:53,507
I'm back.

144
00:10:53,591 --> 00:10:55,301
Oh, you're back?

145
00:10:55,968 --> 00:10:57,011
Ma'am.

146
00:11:01,891 --> 00:11:02,975
Gang-rok,

147
00:11:03,058 --> 00:11:04,643
you got your cast off?

148
00:11:04,727 --> 00:11:09,064
Yes. I know I don't look like it,
but I am in my twenties.

149
00:11:09,148 --> 00:11:10,608
They said I heal super quickly.

150
00:11:12,443 --> 00:11:13,694
That's great.

151
00:11:13,778 --> 00:11:16,655
Right? Now that my foot's back,

152
00:11:17,156 --> 00:11:20,201
you can ask me to run errands
as much as you want.

153
00:11:20,284 --> 00:11:22,578
-Really? Can I do that?
-Of course.

154
00:11:22,661 --> 00:11:24,955
Really? Then can you find me something?

155
00:11:25,039 --> 00:11:27,124
Yes, ma'am! What shall I procure for you?

156
00:11:27,833 --> 00:11:29,335
A house for you.

157
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:36,884
I'd understand if you had lived abroad.

158
00:11:37,510 --> 00:11:40,137
Because there's no specific term
for "reading social cues."

159
00:11:40,221 --> 00:11:42,598
But you were born and raised in Korea.

160
00:11:42,681 --> 00:11:45,559
How long do I have to let you have my man?

161
00:11:45,643 --> 00:11:48,938
I told him to go to your room,
but he was the one who refused.

162
00:11:50,606 --> 00:11:51,816
Then what should you do?

163
00:11:51,899 --> 00:11:55,152
Either shove him into my room by force

164
00:11:55,236 --> 00:11:57,530
or hurry to find a house and move out.

165
00:11:57,613 --> 00:11:58,864
I already found one.

166
00:11:58,948 --> 00:12:00,241
Wait, you did?

167
00:12:00,324 --> 00:12:01,534
I'm moving out tomorrow.

168
00:12:03,369 --> 00:12:04,370
Tomorrow?

169
00:12:04,870 --> 00:12:07,373
Why didn't you say so?

170
00:12:07,456 --> 00:12:09,959
What a shame. Where are you going?

171
00:12:10,042 --> 00:12:11,794
It's a five-minute walk from here.

172
00:12:11,877 --> 00:12:14,171
A five-minute walk? I see.

173
00:12:15,381 --> 00:12:17,758
I'm so sad. What should we do?

174
00:12:17,842 --> 00:12:19,844
Should we have a farewell party?

175
00:12:20,928 --> 00:12:22,304
No need for a farewell party.

176
00:12:22,388 --> 00:12:25,891
Why don't we have some banquet noodles?
Since you seem so keen to celebrate.

177
00:12:27,101 --> 00:12:29,228
Banquet noodles sound perfect.

178
00:12:30,521 --> 00:12:31,564
I'm fine.

179
00:12:32,231 --> 00:12:33,482
You should go now.

180
00:12:33,983 --> 00:12:37,236
Thanks to you, I had a great time today.

181
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:39,280
I'll sleep well tonight.

182
00:12:40,656 --> 00:12:41,699
That's good to hear.

183
00:12:43,242 --> 00:12:46,203
About what I mentioned earlier.

184
00:12:47,746 --> 00:12:48,998
Your marriage.

185
00:12:52,042 --> 00:12:54,628
What I wanted to say about
your marriage was…

186
00:12:54,712 --> 00:12:55,546
Marriage?

187
00:12:55,629 --> 00:12:56,964
I know what you want to say.

188
00:12:57,882 --> 00:12:59,091
Don't worry about it.

189
00:12:59,174 --> 00:13:00,050
Good night.

190
00:13:00,676 --> 00:13:01,510
You too.

191
00:13:12,146 --> 00:13:12,980
Let's go home.

192
00:13:14,523 --> 00:13:15,649
-Okay.
-Okay.

193
00:13:20,529 --> 00:13:22,656
I want to respect her wishes,

194
00:13:23,157 --> 00:13:25,826
so from now on, I'll do my best
to give her happy memories.

195
00:13:28,954 --> 00:13:29,788
Thanks.

196
00:13:32,041 --> 00:13:33,751
For making today great for her.

197
00:13:36,795 --> 00:13:39,214
By the way,
what were you two talking about earlier?

198
00:13:39,298 --> 00:13:40,132
What?

199
00:13:41,091 --> 00:13:45,387
I heard something about marriage.
Does she want us to get married soon?

200
00:13:47,973 --> 00:13:48,807
It's nothing.

201
00:13:51,936 --> 00:13:53,103
Okay.

202
00:13:54,021 --> 00:13:55,105
Marriage?

203
00:13:55,606 --> 00:13:57,775
I guess they're setting a date soon.

204
00:13:57,858 --> 00:13:59,234
How wonderful!

205
00:14:07,493 --> 00:14:11,080
Fine, I'll act clueless.

206
00:14:11,163 --> 00:14:14,041
What else could she have said,
bringing up marriage?

207
00:14:14,124 --> 00:14:16,043
She must have told him
to rush the wedding.

208
00:14:17,336 --> 00:14:19,254
Why is he hiding that from me?

209
00:14:21,048 --> 00:14:22,424
Is he planning to propose?

210
00:14:22,508 --> 00:14:26,303
Should I give him a hint
that a small, pretty bouquet will do?

211
00:14:27,262 --> 00:14:29,974
Wait, so I'm actually getting married?

212
00:14:30,057 --> 00:14:32,851
Oh my God, I'm so happy!

213
00:14:35,437 --> 00:14:36,772
Roses?

214
00:14:37,898 --> 00:14:38,732
Yeah.

215
00:14:38,816 --> 00:14:40,818
All women like roses.

216
00:14:40,901 --> 00:14:44,655
Your grandma loved the flowers yesterday.
You should give her flowers more often.

217
00:14:45,239 --> 00:14:48,033
Baby pink roses are so pretty.

218
00:14:49,159 --> 00:14:50,160
Sure.

219
00:14:50,786 --> 00:14:54,039
She's asking you to buy her flowers
in a roundabout way.

220
00:15:01,630 --> 00:15:02,464
Goodness.

221
00:15:02,965 --> 00:15:06,260
Where are you going with that shovel?

222
00:15:06,343 --> 00:15:09,346
Gang-rok's moving out today,
so I'm helping tidy up his yard.

223
00:15:09,930 --> 00:15:10,889
I see.

224
00:15:11,390 --> 00:15:15,185
So, the soon-to-be bride and groom
will finally be living alone again.

225
00:15:15,978 --> 00:15:17,146
Yes.

226
00:15:17,229 --> 00:15:21,275
Maeng-suk said she heard yesterday
that you two are planning the wedding.

227
00:15:21,859 --> 00:15:23,861
You better tell us the date in advance.

228
00:15:23,944 --> 00:15:25,988
We're all busy people, you know.

229
00:15:27,364 --> 00:15:28,490
That won't happen.

230
00:15:28,574 --> 00:15:29,491
What?

231
00:15:31,660 --> 00:15:32,911
You're not getting married?

232
00:15:34,955 --> 00:15:36,540
We're not. Well, then…

233
00:15:41,879 --> 00:15:42,713
What the…

234
00:15:43,297 --> 00:15:46,925
Maeng-suk said
she clearly heard them yesterday.

235
00:15:52,014 --> 00:15:53,307
I just told you.

236
00:15:53,390 --> 00:15:54,725
-Right.
-But…

237
00:15:54,808 --> 00:15:56,310
-Yes?
-Hui-ja.

238
00:15:57,102 --> 00:15:58,854
The heck's going on?

239
00:15:58,937 --> 00:16:00,064
What is it?

240
00:16:00,147 --> 00:16:01,857
It's about Tae-ha.

241
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:04,985
I just met him,
and he said he's not getting married.

242
00:16:05,069 --> 00:16:06,028
What?

243
00:16:07,780 --> 00:16:11,116
We were actually just talking about that.

244
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:12,034
You were?

245
00:16:12,618 --> 00:16:14,078
The thing is,

246
00:16:14,661 --> 00:16:18,457
I went to Tae-ha's to give him
some boiled pork this morning.

247
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,377
I'm not keeping her around
because I want to.

248
00:16:22,878 --> 00:16:26,256
You know I'm not too fond of them.

249
00:16:27,216 --> 00:16:28,050
But what can I do?

250
00:16:28,717 --> 00:16:31,929
She has nowhere to go and no family.

251
00:16:32,012 --> 00:16:32,846
I feel bad.

252
00:16:33,806 --> 00:16:35,641
I'm just used to having her around now.

253
00:16:38,685 --> 00:16:40,312
Wait. One second.

254
00:16:41,730 --> 00:16:43,023
Hey.

255
00:16:45,776 --> 00:16:47,694
Well, see,

256
00:16:47,778 --> 00:16:50,322
I made some boiled pork
early this morning.

257
00:16:50,405 --> 00:16:52,991
It's good, so I thought I'd…
Do you want to try it?

258
00:16:53,909 --> 00:16:55,369
-Thank you.
-Sure.

259
00:16:55,452 --> 00:16:57,121
-I'll enjoy it.
-Okay.

260
00:16:58,163 --> 00:16:59,623
Go on with what you were doing.

261
00:16:59,706 --> 00:17:00,791
I'll be going.

262
00:17:12,970 --> 00:17:16,056
Now she runs to me whenever she sees me
and doesn't even bark.

263
00:17:16,807 --> 00:17:17,891
She's ours now.

264
00:17:18,934 --> 00:17:22,980
Then I'll bring you some dog food later.

265
00:17:23,564 --> 00:17:24,439
Okay.

266
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:27,234
Good heavens.

267
00:17:27,317 --> 00:17:30,028
Did he really say he took her in
because he felt bad for her,

268
00:17:30,112 --> 00:17:31,864
even though he has no feelings for her?

269
00:17:31,947 --> 00:17:35,284
That's what he said.
I heard it clearly with my own ears.

270
00:17:35,367 --> 00:17:38,787
He went around acting like
Taffy Village's biggest hopeless romantic.

271
00:17:39,371 --> 00:17:41,165
Do you really think Tae-ha would…

272
00:17:41,248 --> 00:17:44,501
-Come on, no way!
-Come on, no way!

273
00:17:52,676 --> 00:17:55,721
I wanted to set the mood
after Gang-rok left,

274
00:17:55,804 --> 00:17:58,849
but all my pajamas are frumpy.

275
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:02,269
BOOST YOUR CURVES AND YOUR CONFIDENCE
PUSH-UP PADS

276
00:18:04,479 --> 00:18:05,647
Well, well.

277
00:18:29,213 --> 00:18:30,047
Hello.

278
00:18:30,130 --> 00:18:31,381
Hello.

279
00:18:32,925 --> 00:18:34,718
Is Tae-ha not around today?

280
00:18:37,221 --> 00:18:38,722
Why do you ask about my man?

281
00:18:38,805 --> 00:18:40,766
You're always together.

282
00:18:41,266 --> 00:18:43,310
I didn't know he was that sweet.

283
00:18:44,770 --> 00:18:47,314
Well, what was he like in school?

284
00:18:48,190 --> 00:18:49,775
Doesn't he tell you about himself?

285
00:18:51,109 --> 00:18:51,944
I'm sure he did.

286
00:18:52,778 --> 00:18:55,530
I'm sure he told me lots.
I just don't remember.

287
00:18:56,031 --> 00:18:59,952
Right, since you don't have your memory,
you must not know much about Tae-ha.

288
00:19:00,786 --> 00:19:04,248
In a way, you must not be that close,
even though he's your boyfriend.

289
00:19:09,378 --> 00:19:12,798
And were you close with him?

290
00:19:13,465 --> 00:19:14,299
Why do you ask?

291
00:19:16,343 --> 00:19:18,387
We're getting married soon, you see.

292
00:19:18,887 --> 00:19:21,515
I was wondering
if I should give you an invitation.

293
00:19:26,603 --> 00:19:28,605
Give me one. I'll be there.

294
00:19:30,399 --> 00:19:31,566
Congratulations.

295
00:19:32,818 --> 00:19:33,652
Thanks.

296
00:19:45,455 --> 00:19:49,293
What is this? Why do I feel sorry for her
all of a sudden?

297
00:19:50,377 --> 00:19:51,378
-Gang-rok.
-Yes?

298
00:19:51,461 --> 00:19:52,296
Take it easy.

299
00:19:52,379 --> 00:19:53,380
Yes, sir.

300
00:19:55,841 --> 00:19:59,094
Sir, I have a question.

301
00:19:59,177 --> 00:20:02,973
Remember the lady that Ms. Go asked me
to take home last time?

302
00:20:03,765 --> 00:20:04,933
What?

303
00:20:07,769 --> 00:20:08,770
Su-ji?

304
00:20:09,563 --> 00:20:10,397
Su-ji…

305
00:20:11,690 --> 00:20:14,568
How do you know her exactly?

306
00:20:15,152 --> 00:20:15,986
A classmate.

307
00:20:17,237 --> 00:20:18,071
A classmate.

308
00:20:18,655 --> 00:20:20,991
She's so pretty.

309
00:20:21,074 --> 00:20:23,327
I keep thinking about her.

310
00:20:23,410 --> 00:20:27,664
So I was wondering if there was
someone on her mind.

311
00:20:29,833 --> 00:20:32,544
I'm not sure.
I don't really know her that well.

312
00:20:34,379 --> 00:20:38,008
Back in your passionate teenage years,
you had a beauty like her as a classmate,

313
00:20:38,091 --> 00:20:39,885
and you didn't feel anything?

314
00:20:44,389 --> 00:20:46,183
How could you even do that?

315
00:20:47,059 --> 00:20:49,269
I don't know.
I've never seen her that way.

316
00:20:50,812 --> 00:20:53,398
-I've never seen her that way.
-Doesn't see her that way?

317
00:20:59,446 --> 00:21:02,949
Then again, you've been devoted
solely to Ms. Go your whole life.

318
00:21:07,579 --> 00:21:10,791
Are you sure
you'll be able to send her away?

319
00:21:19,508 --> 00:21:20,384
I'll send her away

320
00:21:20,967 --> 00:21:22,260
once her memory returns.

321
00:21:24,054 --> 00:21:25,055
I can do it.

322
00:21:26,390 --> 00:21:27,391
I can let her go.

323
00:21:46,451 --> 00:21:49,913
So he's saying he'll send her away
as soon as she gets her memory back,

324
00:21:49,996 --> 00:21:53,125
but since she hasn't,
he's just keeping her around for now?

325
00:21:53,208 --> 00:21:57,003
She has no memory and no family,
so he pities her?

326
00:21:59,214 --> 00:22:01,133
That little rascal!

327
00:22:01,216 --> 00:22:03,093
Tae-ha's just like the rest of them!

328
00:22:03,677 --> 00:22:07,597
If he felt that way, he shouldn't have
doted on her so much.

329
00:22:07,681 --> 00:22:09,266
Damn it!

330
00:22:09,766 --> 00:22:11,476
Why, I ought to just…

331
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,228
Ladies!

332
00:22:15,689 --> 00:22:17,107
I'm here.

333
00:22:23,989 --> 00:22:25,031
Oh no.

334
00:22:26,616 --> 00:22:28,076
Well, this is…

335
00:22:31,788 --> 00:22:33,123
With this,

336
00:22:33,665 --> 00:22:35,125
you could survive a gunshot.

337
00:22:37,043 --> 00:22:40,422
It's just that Gang-rok moved out today.

338
00:22:40,505 --> 00:22:44,676
Since it'll just be the two of us at home,
I've been doing some preparing.

339
00:22:45,260 --> 00:22:47,762
I want to show him a new side of myself.

340
00:22:49,181 --> 00:22:51,266
Come on, you know what I'm talking about.

341
00:22:53,977 --> 00:22:55,479
I can't bear to watch.

342
00:22:56,646 --> 00:23:00,275
I can't do it.
I just want to tell her everything.

343
00:23:03,445 --> 00:23:05,280
-Okay, I'm coming.
-That way.

344
00:23:05,363 --> 00:23:06,656
-Hurry.
-Okay!

345
00:23:06,740 --> 00:23:09,701
-Sit.
-Sit here.

346
00:23:13,205 --> 00:23:16,708
So, what we're saying is,
Tae-ha has no intention of marrying you,

347
00:23:16,791 --> 00:23:19,836
so don't smile at him like that
or give him everything.

348
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:21,379
Have some pride!

349
00:23:22,130 --> 00:23:24,257
He doesn't even see you that way.

350
00:23:24,341 --> 00:23:27,260
Stuffing your chest
like a prize-winning turkey for him

351
00:23:27,344 --> 00:23:29,054
will only make you look ridiculous!

352
00:23:29,137 --> 00:23:32,849
What kind of nonsense
are you all talking about?

353
00:23:32,933 --> 00:23:36,353
You have no idea how much he likes me.

354
00:23:36,853 --> 00:23:39,898
He's only being nice to you
because he feels bad for you, okay?

355
00:23:39,981 --> 00:23:42,776
Because you have no memory
and nowhere else to go.

356
00:23:43,401 --> 00:23:47,989
-Like taking in a stray dog.
-Goodness gracious. Stop it.

357
00:23:48,073 --> 00:23:50,075
This is just breaking my heart.

358
00:23:50,158 --> 00:23:54,829
I can't stand to see our dear Eun-sae
look like a complete fool.

359
00:23:54,913 --> 00:23:59,668
I don't know
what it is you all heard or saw,

360
00:24:00,252 --> 00:24:02,754
but it's all a misunderstanding!

361
00:24:02,837 --> 00:24:05,590
Jang Tae-ha is crazy about me.

362
00:24:07,425 --> 00:24:08,843
So don't worry about me.

363
00:24:10,637 --> 00:24:12,472
We're going to set the date soon,

364
00:24:12,556 --> 00:24:14,766
so come over
and have some banquet noodles.

365
00:24:15,350 --> 00:24:16,184
Well, then,

366
00:24:17,310 --> 00:24:19,354
I'll get going.

367
00:24:19,938 --> 00:24:21,273
Tonight's pretty important.

368
00:24:26,278 --> 00:24:28,947
Don't run. The pads will fall out!

369
00:24:29,030 --> 00:24:31,116
-What do we do?
-What should we do with her?

370
00:24:31,199 --> 00:24:32,576
I feel so bad for her.

371
00:24:32,659 --> 00:24:34,286
What do we do?

372
00:24:34,369 --> 00:24:35,996
-This is insane.
-What to do?

373
00:24:45,797 --> 00:24:48,341
Those ladies are ridiculous.

374
00:24:48,842 --> 00:24:53,221
How could they misunderstand
Jang Tae-ha of all people?

375
00:25:11,364 --> 00:25:12,699
You're home.

376
00:25:16,953 --> 00:25:17,954
Yeah.

377
00:25:47,150 --> 00:25:48,860
I've been waiting for you.

378
00:25:51,488 --> 00:25:52,489
Why?

379
00:25:55,867 --> 00:25:57,452
What do you mean "why"?

380
00:25:58,161 --> 00:26:00,622
Now that Gang-rok has moved out,

381
00:26:01,331 --> 00:26:03,291
we have a lot to do.

382
00:26:04,959 --> 00:26:08,254
We don't have to sleep
in separate rooms anymore,

383
00:26:08,338 --> 00:26:10,965
so we should clean up a bit.

384
00:26:11,466 --> 00:26:13,593
We can use my room as our bedroom.

385
00:26:13,677 --> 00:26:14,844
Right, well…

386
00:26:17,222 --> 00:26:18,682
Some other time.

387
00:26:19,265 --> 00:26:20,767
I'm…

388
00:26:21,267 --> 00:26:23,436
a bit tired today.

389
00:26:24,604 --> 00:26:25,563
So…

390
00:26:26,940 --> 00:26:28,608
cleaning will be a little…

391
00:26:33,279 --> 00:26:34,114
No…

392
00:26:36,700 --> 00:26:37,826
I mean…

393
00:26:39,828 --> 00:26:42,288
that's not the only thing
I was talking about.

394
00:26:49,087 --> 00:26:51,631
Wait, where did the dog go?

395
00:26:53,717 --> 00:26:56,720
Our dog isn't in the yard.

396
00:26:57,429 --> 00:27:01,057
I'll go find her right away.

397
00:27:04,769 --> 00:27:06,396
I'll be right back.

398
00:27:13,319 --> 00:27:14,154
The dog?

399
00:27:19,451 --> 00:27:21,119
She's just going to…

400
00:27:21,703 --> 00:27:23,371
If she comes on hard like that, I…

401
00:27:32,505 --> 00:27:36,468
Does someone who's tired
run out like that to find a dog?

402
00:27:38,970 --> 00:27:41,139
He's definitely dodging me on purpose.

403
00:27:41,723 --> 00:27:43,266
But why?

404
00:27:46,144 --> 00:27:48,229
He doesn't even see you that way.

405
00:27:48,313 --> 00:27:51,191
Stuffing your chest
like a prize-winning turkey for him

406
00:27:51,274 --> 00:27:53,109
will only make you look ridiculous!

407
00:27:58,448 --> 00:27:59,532
No, it can't be.

408
00:28:00,575 --> 00:28:01,826
That's impossible.

409
00:28:02,619 --> 00:28:04,621
I liked you from the moment I saw you.

410
00:28:13,630 --> 00:28:15,048
Yeah.

411
00:28:15,965 --> 00:28:18,635
His eyes weren't lying.

412
00:28:20,595 --> 00:28:22,013
Silly me.

413
00:28:22,096 --> 00:28:25,475
What am I thinking? Dummy.

414
00:28:36,903 --> 00:28:38,404
Don't disappear on me again.

415
00:28:40,114 --> 00:28:42,033
Just don't disappear without a word.

416
00:28:44,244 --> 00:28:46,120
He's only being nice because he feels bad.

417
00:28:46,204 --> 00:28:48,373
Like taking in a stray dog.

418
00:28:53,586 --> 00:28:54,838
This won't do.

419
00:29:05,223 --> 00:29:07,100
Good thing I went looking for her.

420
00:29:07,183 --> 00:29:09,894
She was stuck in a ditch on a farm.

421
00:29:12,105 --> 00:29:13,690
That was a close call.

422
00:29:15,066 --> 00:29:16,609
Won't we sleep together tonight?

423
00:29:17,819 --> 00:29:19,487
-What?
-Answer me.

424
00:29:20,071 --> 00:29:20,989
Right…

425
00:29:21,656 --> 00:29:23,032
Well…

426
00:29:24,242 --> 00:29:25,910
I'm a bit

427
00:29:26,411 --> 00:29:27,245
tired today.

428
00:29:29,122 --> 00:29:31,165
Tae-ha has no intention of marrying you,

429
00:29:31,249 --> 00:29:34,794
so don't smile at him like that
or give him everything.

430
00:29:37,589 --> 00:29:38,840
What about our marriage?

431
00:29:40,675 --> 00:29:42,176
Is that not

432
00:29:43,052 --> 00:29:43,887
happening?

433
00:29:47,640 --> 00:29:48,641
About that…

434
00:29:52,228 --> 00:29:53,813
Let's talk about that…

435
00:29:55,315 --> 00:29:56,524
after you regain your memory.

436
00:29:56,608 --> 00:29:57,483
Why?

437
00:29:57,567 --> 00:29:59,694
You haven't gotten
your memory back yet, and--

438
00:29:59,777 --> 00:30:02,655
What does that have to do with
getting my memory back?

439
00:30:02,739 --> 00:30:05,867
You said we were planning on
getting married!

440
00:30:06,576 --> 00:30:07,535
Still,

441
00:30:08,494 --> 00:30:09,829
getting your memory back

442
00:30:11,122 --> 00:30:12,165
comes first.

443
00:30:25,595 --> 00:30:28,431
You should've told me

444
00:30:28,514 --> 00:30:32,810
that you were living with me
because you felt bad for me.

445
00:30:36,147 --> 00:30:39,567
You were so nice to me

446
00:30:39,651 --> 00:30:41,819
when you never even saw me that way.

447
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:46,574
And you even kissed me, damn you!

448
00:30:49,702 --> 00:30:51,496
Why did you do that?

449
00:30:52,080 --> 00:30:53,081
Why?

450
00:31:07,136 --> 00:31:08,304
Are you going somewhere?

451
00:31:11,724 --> 00:31:13,810
I'm going to meet the S.E.S ladies.

452
00:31:13,893 --> 00:31:15,061
Now?

453
00:31:17,313 --> 00:31:18,481
I'll walk you.

454
00:31:20,024 --> 00:31:20,942
It's fine.

455
00:31:21,025 --> 00:31:23,236
I'm not like the dog,

456
00:31:23,736 --> 00:31:25,780
so I can find my way home just fine.

457
00:31:39,669 --> 00:31:41,170
She seems mad.

458
00:31:58,021 --> 00:31:59,772
We're getting married soon, you see.

459
00:31:59,856 --> 00:32:02,900
I was wondering
if I should give you an invitation.

460
00:32:13,703 --> 00:32:15,663
What are you doing here?

461
00:32:19,167 --> 00:32:20,501
Min Su-ji.

462
00:32:22,837 --> 00:32:26,174
How long are you going to keep this up?
Just work at the clinic.

463
00:32:26,257 --> 00:32:29,260
And you can just keep dating me.
What's the problem?

464
00:32:29,343 --> 00:32:30,803
Do you really not know?

465
00:32:30,887 --> 00:32:31,763
I don't.

466
00:32:31,846 --> 00:32:33,264
I have no idea.

467
00:32:33,347 --> 00:32:35,767
I don't see why you're making
a huge deal out of this.

468
00:32:35,850 --> 00:32:38,811
And I don't know what I have to do
to make you feel better.

469
00:32:38,895 --> 00:32:42,482
Go Eun-sae was moved to tears
when Jang Tae-ha gave her a pair of socks,

470
00:32:42,565 --> 00:32:45,777
but I have no clue what to do
to make you feel satisfied.

471
00:32:50,198 --> 00:32:51,032
What?

472
00:32:51,949 --> 00:32:53,034
What is it?

473
00:32:54,869 --> 00:32:57,663
Tae-ha and Ms. Go are getting married.

474
00:32:58,790 --> 00:32:59,624
They are?

475
00:32:59,707 --> 00:33:03,711
Why do you think she's marrying Tae-ha
when she doesn't even remember him?

476
00:33:04,462 --> 00:33:06,047
Jang Tae-ha is sincere.

477
00:33:07,173 --> 00:33:08,800
Do you even know how to be sincere?

478
00:33:10,301 --> 00:33:11,135
Why wouldn't I?

479
00:33:11,969 --> 00:33:14,097
Hey, I'm sincere too. Toward you.

480
00:33:16,224 --> 00:33:18,017
Sincerity isn't spoken.

481
00:33:18,726 --> 00:33:20,144
You can see it.

482
00:33:23,106 --> 00:33:24,982
Let's stop this, An Gi-jun.

483
00:33:30,655 --> 00:33:32,365
Oh, come on.

484
00:33:33,491 --> 00:33:34,951
Come on!

485
00:33:35,034 --> 00:33:36,244
Damn it.

486
00:33:39,997 --> 00:33:43,084
Why is Go Eun-sae getting married
without even checking the facts?

487
00:33:43,167 --> 00:33:44,001
Is she crazy?

488
00:33:46,796 --> 00:33:48,714
Hello, Ms. Go. Are you and Tae-ha really…

489
00:33:49,715 --> 00:33:50,591
Hello?

490
00:33:51,717 --> 00:33:53,553
What the heck's up with her?

491
00:34:04,564 --> 00:34:06,566
-You're here.
-What's going on?

492
00:34:08,067 --> 00:34:09,527
You had four bottles alone?

493
00:34:10,236 --> 00:34:12,155
They just sort of piled up.

494
00:34:13,322 --> 00:34:14,824
-All this?
-Need an extra glass?

495
00:34:14,907 --> 00:34:16,033
No, I'm good.

496
00:34:16,117 --> 00:34:17,118
Hey.

497
00:34:17,994 --> 00:34:19,912
I heard you're marrying Tae-ha.

498
00:34:20,454 --> 00:34:23,332
Are you sure you won't regret it?
Are you not going to Seoul?

499
00:34:25,835 --> 00:34:27,378
Married?

500
00:34:32,466 --> 00:34:34,427
The thing is, Doctor,

501
00:34:34,510 --> 00:34:36,971
I like Jang Tae-ha.

502
00:34:38,014 --> 00:34:42,143
I really, truly like him.

503
00:34:43,936 --> 00:34:44,770
So what?

504
00:34:44,854 --> 00:34:47,773
He shouldn't have made me fall for him.

505
00:34:48,274 --> 00:34:51,694
What am I supposed to do
if he makes me like him this much

506
00:34:51,777 --> 00:34:55,031
and then goes and does that?

507
00:34:55,615 --> 00:34:57,575
What am I supposed to do?

508
00:35:01,913 --> 00:35:04,373
And what am I supposed to do?
I'm calling Jang Tae-ha.

509
00:35:05,166 --> 00:35:06,792
-No, please.
-You drank too much.

510
00:35:07,293 --> 00:35:09,086
-Don't.
-Why not?

511
00:35:09,170 --> 00:35:13,424
He'll hate me even more
if he sees me like this.

512
00:35:14,008 --> 00:35:15,801
Don't you dare call him.

513
00:35:19,222 --> 00:35:20,514
Give me that.

514
00:35:21,098 --> 00:35:24,101
Wait, don't put that in there…

515
00:35:24,810 --> 00:35:25,937
Seriously?

516
00:35:27,396 --> 00:35:30,733
Why is everyone…
What do you expect me to do?

517
00:35:53,130 --> 00:35:55,508
What's taking her so long?

518
00:36:07,019 --> 00:36:08,271
Here.

519
00:36:12,316 --> 00:36:13,150
Almost there.

520
00:36:13,234 --> 00:36:14,860
What on earth happened?

521
00:36:15,778 --> 00:36:18,239
-She said she was meeting the ladies.
-Take her.

522
00:36:20,658 --> 00:36:21,617
Careful.

523
00:36:26,622 --> 00:36:28,124
She was drinking alone.

524
00:36:28,833 --> 00:36:30,793
Alone? Why would she…

525
00:36:30,876 --> 00:36:33,129
She wouldn't let me call
in case it bothered you.

526
00:36:33,212 --> 00:36:34,964
And she has my phone.

527
00:36:36,090 --> 00:36:37,133
In her back pocket.

528
00:36:44,849 --> 00:36:45,766
Well,

529
00:36:46,475 --> 00:36:47,435
since I'm here,

530
00:36:47,935 --> 00:36:50,313
let me ask you straight out.

531
00:36:51,314 --> 00:36:53,482
Are you really her boyfriend?

532
00:36:54,817 --> 00:36:58,154
If you set out to, it'd be easy
to trick someone who has no memory.

533
00:36:58,738 --> 00:37:02,074
You were a gangster,
so I bet it wouldn't be beneath you.

534
00:37:03,451 --> 00:37:07,121
Why does Ms. Go trust you so much
when she remembers nothing?

535
00:37:07,204 --> 00:37:09,081
How did you get her

536
00:37:09,165 --> 00:37:11,375
so taken with you
without a shred of proof?

537
00:37:11,459 --> 00:37:12,585
Not just her, everyone!

538
00:37:22,845 --> 00:37:25,181
I appreciate you bringing her here,

539
00:37:26,724 --> 00:37:28,309
but watch what you say.

540
00:37:38,944 --> 00:37:39,862
Let's go.

541
00:37:47,203 --> 00:37:48,913
Jang Tae-ha is sincere.

542
00:37:48,996 --> 00:37:51,040
Jang Tae-ha is real.

543
00:37:52,208 --> 00:37:53,167
And if it's all fake?

544
00:37:56,462 --> 00:37:58,089
What will you do if it's all a lie?

545
00:38:12,395 --> 00:38:13,229
Yes?

546
00:38:14,688 --> 00:38:17,191
-You're who?
-Someone who knows Ms. Go Ji-won well.

547
00:38:17,274 --> 00:38:18,484
Ji-won?

548
00:38:19,360 --> 00:38:20,945
Where is she right now?

549
00:38:21,028 --> 00:38:23,531
I'm actually hoping to meet you
regarding that matter.

550
00:38:24,115 --> 00:38:26,784
Could you spare me some time?

551
00:38:31,789 --> 00:38:33,374
Was it around ten years ago?

552
00:38:33,874 --> 00:38:36,752
When we took over
the Hijikata faction in Osaka,

553
00:38:37,378 --> 00:38:41,215
their chairman gifted me this guy,
along with a warning.

554
00:38:42,508 --> 00:38:47,346
"Arowanas still have the instinct to jump
from when they hunted in the wild,

555
00:38:48,472 --> 00:38:50,391
so make sure
to cover the top of the tank."

556
00:38:51,100 --> 00:38:54,770
He warned that the moment I opened the lid

557
00:38:55,604 --> 00:38:58,023
to give him some air…

558
00:39:07,241 --> 00:39:09,243
he'd splash water like this.

559
00:39:09,326 --> 00:39:10,953
He'll be a great athlete.

560
00:39:11,036 --> 00:39:13,205
GOLD MEDAL HOPEFUL JANG TAE-HA
WINS NATIONAL TEAM TRIALS

561
00:39:19,670 --> 00:39:24,675
Like this guy, Jang Tae-ha was a trophy
I was rather proud of.

562
00:39:28,971 --> 00:39:31,182
But if a trophy splashes me with water,

563
00:39:31,807 --> 00:39:32,933
I don't need it anymore.

564
00:39:43,068 --> 00:39:44,153
Chairman, wait.

565
00:39:44,236 --> 00:39:45,488
Sir!

566
00:40:05,132 --> 00:40:05,966
Sir.

567
00:40:07,426 --> 00:40:08,427
Sir?

568
00:40:42,962 --> 00:40:43,879
Jang Tae-ha.

569
00:40:45,464 --> 00:40:46,382
Find him.

570
00:40:47,299 --> 00:40:48,133
Yes, sir.

571
00:40:55,808 --> 00:40:57,893
Easy. Careful.

572
00:41:00,563 --> 00:41:02,231
Let go.

573
00:41:03,399 --> 00:41:04,441
I thought…

574
00:41:05,276 --> 00:41:08,904
You said you were meeting the ladies.
Why did you drink alone?

575
00:41:08,988 --> 00:41:11,782
And you should have called me
if you were drunk.

576
00:41:19,415 --> 00:41:20,249
Why?

577
00:41:21,083 --> 00:41:23,002
Because I'm your boyfriend…

578
00:41:23,502 --> 00:41:24,503
Liar.

579
00:41:26,380 --> 00:41:28,132
I know everything now.

580
00:41:30,634 --> 00:41:31,760
Know what?

581
00:41:36,473 --> 00:41:37,683
You see,

582
00:41:38,684 --> 00:41:40,686
I found out about everything.

583
00:41:42,438 --> 00:41:43,731
What do you…

584
00:41:55,075 --> 00:41:55,993
You don't mean…

585
00:41:58,037 --> 00:41:58,871
Yeah.

586
00:42:00,956 --> 00:42:06,629
What kind of person Jang Tae-ha really is.

587
00:42:06,712 --> 00:42:08,631
I know everything now.

588
00:42:12,718 --> 00:42:13,886
So

589
00:42:14,970 --> 00:42:17,431
you don't have to pretend
to like me anymore.

590
00:42:22,227 --> 00:42:23,062
Go Eun-sae.

591
00:42:26,357 --> 00:42:27,232
Your memory.

592
00:42:29,318 --> 00:42:30,444
Is it back?

593
00:42:36,158 --> 00:42:39,119
Even if I'd lost my memory,

594
00:42:39,703 --> 00:42:43,499
how could you lie to me
about something like that?

595
00:42:47,795 --> 00:42:50,214
You shouldn't have done that to me.

596
00:43:28,168 --> 00:43:30,462
HONG'S BOXING GYM

597
00:43:30,546 --> 00:43:32,089
Hey, Tae-ha.

598
00:43:32,589 --> 00:43:33,674
She says it's back.

599
00:43:35,384 --> 00:43:36,677
Go Eun-sae's memory.

600
00:43:37,261 --> 00:43:39,847
She says she's got it all back.

601
00:43:49,148 --> 00:43:52,317
It's a relief that her memory came back
before we could get her out of here.

602
00:43:56,905 --> 00:44:01,076
Maybe she drank
because she was so shocked.

603
00:44:08,500 --> 00:44:11,420
Well, now that she remembers everything,

604
00:44:11,503 --> 00:44:14,214
she'll know she has to leave Korea
in order to survive.

605
00:44:15,424 --> 00:44:18,343
All that's left
is for her to leave safely.

606
00:44:28,103 --> 00:44:29,480
Are you okay?

607
00:44:35,527 --> 00:44:37,571
Now that her memory's back,

608
00:44:38,405 --> 00:44:40,032
this whole act is over.

609
00:44:40,616 --> 00:44:43,160
Pretending to be her boyfriend,
being all close…

610
00:44:44,077 --> 00:44:45,788
That all stops tomorrow.

611
00:44:49,416 --> 00:44:50,542
Well,

612
00:44:52,211 --> 00:44:54,129
I was never her real boyfriend anyway.

613
00:44:55,088 --> 00:44:57,758
That doesn't mean
your feelings were fake too.

614
00:45:06,475 --> 00:45:10,938
It meant I could keep her safe by my side.
That's all that matters.

615
00:45:15,275 --> 00:45:16,360
Look.

616
00:45:17,361 --> 00:45:19,488
Since things have come to this,

617
00:45:19,571 --> 00:45:22,908
why don't you just go to Japan
with Prosecutor Go?

618
00:45:24,326 --> 00:45:28,539
Just go, turn a blind eye to everything,
and spend the rest of your lives together.

619
00:45:35,295 --> 00:45:37,089
How could I leave Grandma behind?

620
00:45:40,008 --> 00:45:42,010
I'm well aware of that too.

621
00:45:43,428 --> 00:45:45,138
But for once in your life,

622
00:45:45,222 --> 00:45:47,933
you should be allowed to be selfish
and do what you want.

623
00:45:52,062 --> 00:45:53,063
I'm fine.

624
00:45:55,399 --> 00:45:57,526
Once she's smuggled out,
it's really goodbye.

625
00:45:57,609 --> 00:46:00,195
I say this because once she's gone,
that'll really be it.

626
00:46:00,279 --> 00:46:02,990
I told you, I'm fine.

627
00:46:13,125 --> 00:46:14,710
I'm really okay.

628
00:46:19,506 --> 00:46:20,966
Oh boy.

629
00:46:24,177 --> 00:46:25,554
They cheated in this match.

630
00:46:26,763 --> 00:46:29,808
It was nice meeting you,
Mr. Future Gold Medalist.

631
00:46:54,750 --> 00:46:55,667
This one's for real.

632
00:47:15,395 --> 00:47:16,355
Hey, hold on tight.

633
00:47:52,349 --> 00:47:54,267
This must be why I liked you.

634
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:02,002
Even if I can't do much else for you,

635
00:49:02,502 --> 00:49:04,212
on hard days like tonight,

636
00:49:04,921 --> 00:49:07,883
I thought I could at least shield you
from the rain.

637
00:49:08,467 --> 00:49:10,302
I really wanted to do that for you.

638
00:49:15,140 --> 00:49:19,102
Are you thinking of marrying that girl?

639
00:49:19,686 --> 00:49:23,106
I know you like her a lot.

640
00:49:26,234 --> 00:49:29,738
She has to leave soon.

641
00:49:32,741 --> 00:49:34,409
That's the only way she can live.

642
00:49:34,493 --> 00:49:36,036
What are you talking about?

643
00:49:36,620 --> 00:49:38,955
Where would she go without you?

644
00:49:40,791 --> 00:49:42,626
I can't explain everything,

645
00:49:43,293 --> 00:49:45,295
but she has to go.

646
00:50:21,998 --> 00:50:23,667
OUR STICKY LOVE

647
00:51:10,297 --> 00:51:14,259
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi

